I stand near the wooden counter.
I look at the elderly man.
I ask him politely.
"Sir, is a cutting chai available here?"
"And is a bun maska available too?"
The elderly man smiles.
He nods his head happily.
He says to me.
"Yes, everything is available here."
I say, "Excellent."
"Please give one cutting chai."
"Please give one bun maska too."
The man says, "Okay, madam."
"Please go inside."
"Sit near a table there."
"Please wait a little."
I say, "Thank you, sir."
I go inside.
